<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  PROBE E5. E4's SERVICE-SIDE TWIN: a <decisionService> whose @name equals a
  <decision>'s @name.

  tDecisionService is a tInvocable, and on KIE its name lives in the same FEEL
  scope that makes probe D2's `bundle(n: ...)` resolve. So a service name can
  collide with a decision name in exactly the way a BKM name can, and section 5.2's
  scope list does not yet mention either.

      decision        bundle  = n + 5
      decisionService bundle  = { output: total, encapsulated: step, input: n }
      decision        read_bundle = bundle + 1

  The service is GROUPING-ONLY: nothing carries a knowledgeRequirement to it.
  That is deliberate, so that the Camunda leg can run at all; a KR to a service
  is a whole-file ClassCastException there (probe D2), which would mask this
  question behind that one.

  On Camunda a service is unaddressable, so the only question its leg answers is
  whether the colliding name perturbs the parse or the decisions. On KIE the
  question is sharper: does `bundle` in read_bundle resolve to the decision's
  value or to the invocable, and does anything say so.

  MEASURED 2026-07-31:
    KIE 8.44  : validator raises DUPLICATE_NAME twice (decision node and service
                node). Build clean. RUNTIME IS ENTIRELY UNAFFECTED: all four
                decisions answer correctly, `bundle` in read_bundle resolves to
                the DECISION, and evaluateDecisionService("bundle") still reaches
                the service and prints `SVC bundle -> {n=4, total=9}`. So on the
                service side the collision is a VALIDATOR-ONLY event.
    Camunda 8 : silent; all four decisions correct.

  Contrast probe E4 sharply. A BKM name colliding with a decision name DELETES
  the decision on KIE; a SERVICE name colliding with a decision name costs a
  validator message and nothing else. Same diagnostic code, different severity in
  fact. That is why the two probes are separate files.

  Wired HarnessMustFail on the KIE leg (the validator errors alone fail the
  banner) and HarnessMustPass on the Camunda leg.
-->
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" id="definitions_collide_svc_decision" name="collide_svc_decision" namespace="https://legalese.com/l4/dmn/collide_svc_decision" exporter="hand">
  <inputData id="input_n" name="n">
    <variable id="input_n_var" name="n" typeRef="number"/>
  </inputData>
  <decision id="decision_step" name="step">
    <variable id="decision_step_var" name="step" typeRef="number"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_step_n">
      <requiredInput href="#input_n"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_step_lit">
      <text>n * 2</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
  <decision id="decision_total" name="total">
    <variable id="decision_total_var" name="total" typeRef="number"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_total_step">
      <requiredDecision href="#decision_step"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_total_lit">
      <text>step + 1</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
  <decision id="decision_bundle" name="bundle">
    <variable id="decision_bundle_var" name="bundle" typeRef="number"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_bundle_n">
      <requiredInput href="#input_n"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_bundle_lit">
      <text>n + 5</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
  <decision id="decision_read_bundle" name="read_bundle">
    <variable id="decision_read_bundle_var" name="read_bundle" typeRef="number"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_read_bundle">
      <requiredDecision href="#decision_bundle"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_read_bundle_lit">
      <text>bundle + 1</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
  <decisionService id="svc_bundle" name="bundle">
    <variable id="svc_bundle_var" name="bundle" typeRef="number"/>
    <outputDecision href="#decision_total"/>
    <encapsulatedDecision href="#decision_step"/>
    <inputData href="#input_n"/>
  </decisionService>
</definitions>
